/-!
# The SAGBI criterion for monic families

Let `m` be a monomial order on `σ →₀ ℕ` and let `c : ι → MvPolynomial σ k` be a family of monic
polynomials over a field, with leading exponents `a i = m.degree (c i)`. Write
`A w = ∑ i, w i • a i` (`Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a w`) for the exponent map, and `φ = aeval c`
for the substitution `Y i ↦ c i` of polynomials in variables `Y i`, `i : ι`. The image
`φ (Y^w) = ∏ i, c i ^ w i` is monic with leading exponent `A w`. Its leading term `X^(A w)` is the
image of `Y^w` under the substitution `Y i ↦ X^(a i)` of the leading monomials, whose kernel is the
toric ideal `TauCeti.toricIdeal k a`.

Choose binomials `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` generating the toric ideal. The images of their two monomials
under `φ` have the same leading monomial `X^(A (u j))`, which cancels. The **SAGBI criterion**
states that `c` is a SAGBI basis of the subalgebra `k[c]` it generates if and only if each image
`φ (Y^(u j) - Y^(v j))` has a *bounded zero subduction*: a polynomial `Q` in the variables `Y i`
with `φ Q = φ (Y^(u j) - Y^(v j))` all of whose exponents `w` satisfy `A w ≺ A (u j)`. When the
image is zero this holds with `Q = 0`; no inequality is asserted for the degree of the zero
polynomial. The finite certificates `Q` are the input to the presentation of `k[c]` and to the
flat degeneration of `k[c]` to the semigroup algebra of its initial algebra.

## Main results

* `MonomialOrder.weightedHomogeneousComponent_mem_toricIdeal`: if all exponents `w` of `P` have
  `A w ≼ e` and the coefficient of `X^e` in `φ P` vanishes, then the part of `P` of weight `e`
  lies in the toric ideal.
* `MonomialOrder.IsSAGBIBasis.exists_aeval_eq_aeval_sub`: if `c` is a SAGBI basis of `k[c]`, then
  every binomial `Y^u - Y^v` with `A u = A v` has a bounded zero subduction.
* `MonomialOrder.exists_aeval_eq_of_mem_toricIdeal`: if the generating binomials have bounded zero
  subductions, then so does every element of the toric ideal all of whose exponents have the same
  image under `A`.
* `MonomialOrder.isSAGBIBasis_range_iff_forall_exists_aeval_eq`: **the SAGBI criterion**.

## Implementation notes

Sufficiency is a well-founded induction on the largest value `δ` of `A` on the exponents of a
representation `f = φ P` of a nonzero element of `k[c]`. If the coefficients of `P` at the
exponents `w` with `A w = δ` have nonzero sum, then `f` has leading exponent `δ`, which lies in
the monoid generated by the `a i`. Otherwise the part of `P` of weight `δ` lies in the toric
ideal. The weight-`δ` component of its expression through the generating binomials is a sum of
multiples of the binomials of weight exactly `δ`, and replacing each binomial by its bounded zero
subduction gives a representation of `f` with smaller `δ`.

## References

* B. Sturmfels, *Gröbner Bases and Convex Polytopes*, University Lecture Series 8, AMS, 1996,
  Chapter 11.
* L. Robbiano, M. Sweedler, *Subalgebra bases*, in *Commutative Algebra (Salvador, 1988)*,
  Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1430, Springer, 1990, 61–87.
* Bruns, Conca, Lembo, arXiv:2504.10019, §2, Theorem 2.2 and Proposition 2.4, for monic SAGBI
  families and bounded subduction.
-/

public section

open MvPolynomial

namespace MonomialOrder

variable {σ ι : Type*} {m : MonomialOrder σ}

section CommSemiring

variable {R : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [Nontrivial R] {c : ι → MvPolynomial σ R}

/-- Let `c` be a monic family and write `A w = ∑ i, w i • m.degree (c i)`. If every exponent `w` of
`P` satisfies `A w ≼ δ` and the coefficient of `X^δ` in `aeval c P` vanishes, then the part of `P`
of weight `δ` for the weights `m.degree (c i)` lies in the toric ideal of the leading exponents of
`c`: the cancelling top part of `P` is a relation among the leading monomials. -/
theorem weightedHomogeneousComponent_mem_toricIdeal (hc : ∀ i, m.Monic (c i))
    {P : MvPolynomial ι R} {δ : σ →₀ ℕ}
    (hP : ∀ w ∈ P.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≼[m] δ)
    (hδ : (aeval c P).coeff δ = 0) :
    weightedHomogeneousComponent (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) δ P ∈
      TauCeti.toricIdeal R (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) := by
  classical
  have hA (w : ι →₀ ℕ) : Finsupp.weight (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w =
      Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w := by
    rw [Finsupp.weight_apply, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply]
  rw [coeff_aeval_of_forall_le hc hP] at hδ
  rw [TauCeti.mem_toricIdeal_iff, weightedHomogeneousComponent_apply, map_sum]
  simp_rw [TauCeti.aeval_single_monomial, single_eq_monomial]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (g := fun w ↦ monomial δ (P.coeff w)) fun w hw ↦ by
    rw [← hA, (Finset.mem_filter.1 hw).2], ← map_sum]
  simp only [hA]
  rw [hδ, map_zero]

end CommSemiring

section CommRing

variable {R J : Type*} [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R] {c : ι → MvPolynomial σ R}

/-- Let `c` be a family of polynomials and write `A w = ∑ i, w i • m.degree (c i)`. Suppose that
binomials `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` generate the toric ideal of the leading exponents of `c` and that
the image of each under `aeval c` is the image of a polynomial all of whose exponents `w` satisfy
`A w ≺ A (u j)`. Then every element `p` of the toric ideal all of whose exponents `w` satisfy
`A w = δ` has the same image as a polynomial all of whose exponents `w` satisfy `A w ≺ δ`. -/
theorem exists_aeval_eq_of_mem_toricIdeal {u v : J → ι →₀ ℕ}
    (hJ : TauCeti.toricIdeal R (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ monomial (u j) (1 : R) - monomial (v j) 1))
    (hQ : ∀ j, ∃ Q : MvPolynomial ι R,
      aeval c Q = aeval c (monomial (u j) (1 : R) - monomial (v j) 1) ∧
      ∀ w ∈ Q.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≺[m]
        Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) (u j))
    {p : MvPolynomial ι R} (hp : p ∈ TauCeti.toricIdeal R (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i))) {δ : σ →₀ ℕ}
    (hpδ : ∀ w ∈ p.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w = δ) :
    ∃ p' : MvPolynomial ι R, aeval c p' = aeval c p ∧
      ∀ w ∈ p'.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≺[m] δ := by
  classical
  set a := fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)
  set A := Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a
  have hA (w : ι →₀ ℕ) : Finsupp.weight a w = A w := by
    rw [Finsupp.weight_apply, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply]
  choose Q hQc hQlt using hQ
  -- The generating binomial `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` is weighted homogeneous of weight `A (u j)`.
  have hβ (j : J) :
      (monomial (u j) (1 : R) - monomial (v j) 1).IsWeightedHomogeneous a (A (u j)) := by
    have hmem : monomial (u j) (1 : R) - monomial (v j) 1 ∈ TauCeti.toricIdeal R a := by
      rw [hJ]
      exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩
    have huv : A (u j) = A (v j) := TauCeti.monomial_sub_monomial_mem_toricIdeal_iff.1 hmem
    exact (isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial _ _ _ (hA _)).sub
      (isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial _ _ _ ((hA _).trans huv.symm))
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := Finsupp.mem_ideal_span_range_iff_exists_finsupp.1 (hJ ▸ hp)
  -- The weight-`δ` component of `p = ∑ j, g j * (Y^(u j) - Y^(v j))` is `p` itself; it is the sum
  -- of the multiples `h j * (Y^(u j) - Y^(v j))` by the components `h j` of weight `δ - A (u j)`.
  set h : J → MvPolynomial ι R := fun j ↦
    if A (u j) ≤ δ then weightedHomogeneousComponent a (δ - A (u j)) (g j) else 0
  have hph : p = ∑ j ∈ g.support, h j * (monomial (u j) 1 - monomial (v j) 1) := by
    have hpw : p.IsWeightedHomogeneous a δ := fun w hw ↦ (hA w).trans (hpδ w (mem_support_iff.2 hw))
    rw [← weightedHomogeneousComponent_eq_self hpw, ← hg, Finsupp.sum, map_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ ↦ ?_
    rw [(hβ j).weightedHomogeneousComponent_mul_right]
    split_ifs <;> simp [h, *]
  refine ⟨∑ j ∈ g.support, h j * Q j, ?_, fun w hw ↦ ?_⟩
  · simp_rw [hph, map_sum, map_mul, hQc]
  -- An exponent of `h j * Q j` is a sum `x + y` with `A x = δ - A (u j)` and `A y ≺ A (u j)`.
  obtain ⟨j, -, hj⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.1 (support_sum hw)
  obtain ⟨x, hx, y, hy, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_add.1 (support_mul _ _ hj)
  have hle : A (u j) ≤ δ := by
    by_contra hle
    simp [h, hle] at hx
  have hAx : A x = δ - A (u j) := by
    rw [← hA]
    simp only [h, hle, ite_true] at hx
    exact weightedHomogeneousComponent_isWeightedHomogeneous _ _ (mem_support_iff.1 hx)
  rw [map_add, map_add, hAx]
  conv_rhs => rw [← tsub_add_cancel_of_le hle, map_add]
  exact add_lt_add_right (hQlt j y hy) _

end CommRing

section Field

variable {k J : Type*} [Field k] {c : ι → MvPolynomial σ k}

/-- **Necessity in the SAGBI criterion.** Let `c` be a monic family which is a SAGBI basis of the
subalgebra it generates, and write `A w = ∑ i, w i • m.degree (c i)`. If `A u = A v`, then the image
of `Y^u - Y^v` under `aeval c` is the image of a polynomial `Q` all of whose exponents `w` satisfy
`A w ≺ A u`. -/
theorem IsSAGBIBasis.exists_aeval_eq_aeval_sub (hc : ∀ i, m.Monic (c i))
    (h : m.IsSAGBIBasis (Set.range c) (Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range c))) {u v : ι →₀ ℕ}
    (huv : Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) u =
      Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) v) :
    ∃ Q : MvPolynomial ι k, aeval c Q = aeval c (monomial u (1 : k) - monomial v 1) ∧
      ∀ w ∈ Q.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≺[m]
        Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) u := by
  have hf : aeval c (monomial u (1 : k) - monomial v 1) ∈
      Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range c) := by
    rw [← aeval_range]
    exact AlgHom.mem_range_self _ _
  simpa only [Function.comp_def] using
    h.exists_aeval_eq_support_lt (fun i ↦ (hc i).ne_zero) hf
      (m.aeval_monomial_sub_monomial_eq_zero_or_degree_lt hc u v
        (by simpa only [Function.comp_def] using huv))

/-- The sufficiency step of the SAGBI criterion, by well-founded induction on an upper bound `δ`
for the values of `A` on the exponents of a representation `f = aeval c P`. -/
private theorem degree_aeval_mem_closure (hc : ∀ i, m.Monic (c i)) {u v : J → ι →₀ ℕ}
    (hJ : TauCeti.toricIdeal k (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ monomial (u j) (1 : k) - monomial (v j) 1))
    (hQ : ∀ j, ∃ Q : MvPolynomial ι k,
      aeval c Q = aeval c (monomial (u j) (1 : k) - monomial (v j) 1) ∧
      ∀ w ∈ Q.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≺[m]
        Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) (u j))
    (δ : σ →₀ ℕ) {P : MvPolynomial ι k}
    (hPδ : ∀ w ∈ P.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≼[m] δ)
    (hP : aeval c P ≠ 0) :
    m.degree (aeval c P) ∈ AddSubmonoid.closure (Set.range fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) := by
  classical
  set a := fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)
  set A := Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a
  have hAmem (w : ι →₀ ℕ) : A w ∈ AddSubmonoid.closure (Set.range a) :=
    AddSubmonoid.mem_closure_range_iff.2 ⟨w, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply ℕ w⟩
  induction hd : m.toSyn δ using WellFoundedLT.induction generalizing δ P with
  | ind d ih =>
  subst hd
  by_cases htop : (aeval c P).coeff δ = 0
  · -- The coefficients of `P` at the exponents of weight `δ` cancel, so its part `P₀` of weight
    -- `δ` lies in the toric ideal and has a representation by exponents of weight below `δ`.
    obtain ⟨P₀, hP₀def⟩ : ∃ P₀, P₀ = weightedHomogeneousComponent a δ P := ⟨_, rfl⟩
    have hA (w : ι →₀ ℕ) : Finsupp.weight a w = A w := by
      rw [Finsupp.weight_apply, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply]
    have hP₀ : P₀ ∈ TauCeti.toricIdeal k a :=
      hP₀def ▸ weightedHomogeneousComponent_mem_toricIdeal hc hPδ htop
    obtain ⟨P₁, hP₁, hP₁δ⟩ := exists_aeval_eq_of_mem_toricIdeal hJ hQ hP₀ fun w hw ↦ by
      rw [← hA]
      rw [hP₀def] at hw
      exact weightedHomogeneousComponent_isWeightedHomogeneous _ _ (mem_support_iff.1 hw)
    -- Replace `P₀` by `P₁` in `P`.
    have hP' : aeval c (P - P₀ + P₁) = aeval c P := by rw [map_add, map_sub, hP₁, sub_add_cancel]
    have hlt : ∀ w ∈ (P - P₀ + P₁).support, A w ≺[m] δ := by
      intro w hw
      rcases Finset.mem_union.1 (support_add hw) with hw | hw
      · rw [mem_support_iff, coeff_sub, hP₀def, coeff_weightedHomogeneousComponent, hA] at hw
        have hwδ : A w ≠ δ := fun h ↦ hw (by simp [h])
        have hwP : w ∈ P.support := mem_support_iff.2 fun h ↦ hw (by simp [h])
        exact lt_of_le_of_ne (hPδ w hwP) fun h ↦ hwδ (m.toSyn.injective h)
      · exact hP₁δ w hw
    have hne : (P - P₀ + P₁).support.Nonempty :=
      support_nonempty.2 fun h ↦ hP (by rw [← hP', h, map_zero])
    obtain ⟨w₀, hw₀, hmax⟩ := Finset.exists_max_image _ (fun w ↦ m.toSyn (A w)) hne
    rw [← hP']
    exact ih _ (hlt w₀ hw₀) (A w₀) (by rwa [hP']) hmax rfl
  · -- Otherwise the leading exponent of `aeval c P` is `δ`, a value of `A`.
    have hdeg : m.degree (aeval c P) = δ := m.toSyn.injective <|
      le_antisymm (degree_aeval_le_of_forall_le hc hPδ) (m.le_degree (mem_support_iff.2 htop))
    rw [coeff_aeval_of_forall_le hc hPδ] at htop
    obtain ⟨w, hw, -⟩ := Finset.exists_ne_zero_of_sum_ne_zero htop
    rw [hdeg, ← (Finset.mem_filter.1 hw).2]
    exact hAmem w

/-- **The SAGBI criterion.** Let `c` be a family of monic polynomials over a field, write
`A w = ∑ i, w i • m.degree (c i)`, and let binomials `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` generate the toric ideal
of the leading exponents of `c`. Then `c` is a SAGBI basis of the subalgebra it generates if and
only if, for every `j`, the image of `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` under `aeval c` is the image of a
polynomial all of whose exponents `w` satisfy `A w ≺ A (u j)`. -/
theorem isSAGBIBasis_range_iff_forall_exists_aeval_eq (hc : ∀ i, m.Monic (c i))
    {u v : J → ι →₀ ℕ}
    (hJ : TauCeti.toricIdeal k (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ monomial (u j) (1 : k) - monomial (v j) 1)) :
    m.IsSAGBIBasis (Set.range c) (Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range c)) ↔
      ∀ j, ∃ Q : MvPolynomial ι k,
        aeval c Q = aeval c (monomial (u j) (1 : k) - monomial (v j) 1) ∧
        ∀ w ∈ Q.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≺[m]
          Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) (u j) := by
  refine ⟨fun h j ↦ h.exists_aeval_eq_aeval_sub hc ?_, fun hQ ↦ ?_⟩
  · refine (TauCeti.monomial_sub_monomial_mem_toricIdeal_iff (R := k)).1 ?_
    rw [hJ]
    exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩
  refine isSAGBIBasis_iff_degree_mem_closure.2 ⟨Algebra.subset_adjoin, fun f hf hf0 ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval] at hf
  obtain ⟨P, rfl⟩ := hf
  have hne : P.support.Nonempty := support_nonempty.2 fun h ↦ hf0 (by rw [h, map_zero])
  obtain ⟨w₀, -, hmax⟩ := Finset.exists_max_image _
    (fun w ↦ m.toSyn (Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w)) hne
  refine AddSubmonoid.closure_mono ?_ (degree_aeval_mem_closure hc hJ hQ _ hmax hf0)
  rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨c i, ⟨⟨i, rfl⟩, (hc i).ne_zero⟩, rfl⟩

end Field

end MonomialOrder
